{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:KnotsParticlesConfinement.ElectroweakHiggsTorusLinkTriplet","@type":"LeanModule","name":"KnotsParticlesConfinement.ElectroweakHiggsTorusLinkTriplet","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":22,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWHiggsTorusLinkTriplet.identification","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWHiggsTorusLinkTriplet.identification","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-higgs-torus-link-triplet.lean#L180-L180","doc":"The identification: crossings `(4, 6, 8)`, with sectors `W, Z` doublets\nand `H` singlet supplied by `EWSectorAssignment` (whence, via\n`thm:ew-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution`, spins `(1,1,0)` and charges\n`(±1, 0, 0)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWHiggsTorusLinkTriplet.crossings","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWHiggsTorusLinkTriplet.crossings","kind":"def","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-higgs-torus-link-triplet.lean#L175-L175","doc":"Crossing counts of the `(W, Z, H)` carrier links. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWHiggsTorusLinkTriplet.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWHiggsTorusLinkTriplet.mk","kind":"ctor","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-higgs-torus-link-triplet.lean#L172-L172","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWHiggsTorusLinkTriplet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWHiggsTorusLinkTriplet","kind":"class","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-higgs-torus-link-triplet.lean#L162-L184","doc":"**C_top (DEPENDENT on C1, C-sector) — the full electroweak identification.**\n\n`W ↔ T(2,4)`, `Z ↔ T(2,6)`, `H ↔ T(2,8)`: crossings `(4, 6, 8)`, with the\nspin sectors supplied by the (open) sector postulate `EWSectorAssignment`.\nCharge and spin themselves are *not* carried here as conjectural fields —\nthey are the proved `thm:ew-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution`. This top\nnode rests on the conjectural selection principle (C1) and the sector\npostulate, so it is a *dependent* conjecture, honestly carrying both as\n`[instance]` binders. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:electroweak-higgs-torus-link-triplet","label":"conj:electroweak-higgs-torus-link-triplet","md":"quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-higgs-torus-link-triplet.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorAssignment.higgs_neutral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorAssignment.higgs_neutral","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-higgs-torus-link-triplet.lean#L160-L160","doc":"`H` (`k = 4`) is the neutral singlet. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorAssignment.z_neutral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorAssignment.z_neutral","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-higgs-torus-link-triplet.lean#L158-L158","doc":"`Z` (`k = 3`) is neutral — via the Weinberg `(W³, B) → (Z, γ)` mixing, not\nvia bar-even membership. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorAssignment.w_charged","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorAssignment.w_charged","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-higgs-torus-link-triplet.lean#L155-L155","doc":"`W` (`k = 2`) is the charged member — the paper's free choice of the\ncharged vector slot (mirror `t3Label 3 = 1` is equally admissible). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorAssignment.t3Label","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorAssignment.t3Label","kind":"def","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-higgs-torus-link-triplet.lean#L152-L152","doc":"Doubled isospin `2·T₃` label of the carrier of twist `k`. This is the\n**free label** (see the class docstring): no proved crossing→charge\nprinciple forces which vector slot is charged. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorAssignment.z_doublet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorAssignment.z_doublet","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-higgs-torus-link-triplet.lean#L148-L148","doc":"`Z` (`k = 3`) is a bar-odd doublet (neutral via mixing, not via `A₊`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorAssignment.w_doublet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorAssignment.w_doublet","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-higgs-torus-link-triplet.lean#L146-L146","doc":"`W` (`k = 2`) is a bar-odd doublet. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorAssignment.higgs_singlet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorAssignment.higgs_singlet","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-higgs-torus-link-triplet.lean#L144-L144","doc":"`H` (`k = 4`) is the bar-even self-dual singlet. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorAssignment.isSinglet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorAssignment.isSinglet","kind":"def","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-higgs-torus-link-triplet.lean#L142-L142","doc":"Spin sector of the carrier of twist `k`: `true` = singlet (`A₊`),\n`false` = doublet (`A₋`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorAssignment.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorAssignment.mk","kind":"ctor","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-higgs-torus-link-triplet.lean#L139-L139","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorAssignment","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorAssignment","kind":"class","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-higgs-torus-link-triplet.lean#L105-L160","doc":"**C-sector (PRIMARY) — the single sector-assignment postulate.**\n\nThis class **replaces the former C3 (charge) and C4 (spin) primary\nconjectures**. It is the one residual physics input beyond selection: the\nassignment of each carrier to a `σ`-spin-involution sector\n(`def:spin-involution`) — the spin-singlet `A₊` (bar-even, neutral) or the\nspin-doublet `A₋` (bar-odd, charged). Once this assignment is fixed, charge\nand spin are **derived**, not postulated: this is the sorry-free\n`thm:ew-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution`\n(`H ∈ A₊ ⇒` scalar+neutral; `W± ∈ A₋ ⇒` vector, `T₃=±1`; `Z ∈ A₋` vector,\nneutral via Weinberg mixing).\n\nTwist convention: `k = 2 ↔ W`, `k = 3 ↔ Z`, `k = 4 ↔ H`.\n\n**The `t3Label` field is a FREE LABEL, not forced (honest, 2026-07-05).**\nWhich of the two *vector* slots (`k = 2 ↔ σ₁⁴` or `k = 3 ↔ σ₃⁶`) hosts the\n*charged* carrier `W±` (`|t₃| = 1`) versus the neutral `Z` (`t₃ = 0`) is\n**not** fixed by any proved crossing→charge principle. The corpus\ncrossing→charge map `def:coulomb-charge` (`Q = ½·writhe`) evaluated on the\nall-positive braid `σ₁^{2k}` gives `Q(T(2,2k)) = k > 0` for *every* carrier,\nso it makes all three charged and cannot select the neutral slot; the\n`writhe → Y` map is falsified, and the one map that survives that audit,\n`writhe → I₃` (`2·I₃ = writhe`), *also* fails here — on the all-positive\ncarriers it gives `2·I₃ = 2k`, nonzero on both vector slots, so it too\nyields no neutral slot (`writheI3_does_not_select_neutral_slot` in\n`thm:ew-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution`;\n`2026-06-02-u1-hypercharge-assignment.md`).\nThe assignment `t3Label 2 = 1` (`W` at the lower crossing `σ₁⁴`) below is the\npaper's *choice*, consistent with the mass ordering `4 < 6 < 8` (necessary,\nnot sufficient); its underdetermination is proved as `which_slot_is_W_free`\nin `thm:ew-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution`. What *would* force it is a\ngenuine crossing/linking → `T₃` map singling out the `Z` slot — an open\ninput the framework does not yet supply. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorEnumeration.carriers_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorEnumeration.carriers_eq","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-higgs-torus-link-triplet.lean#L103-L103","doc":"The carrier set is exactly `{2, 3, 4}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorEnumeration.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorEnumeration.mk","kind":"ctor","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-higgs-torus-link-triplet.lean#L101-L101","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorEnumeration","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSectorEnumeration","kind":"class","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-higgs-torus-link-triplet.lean#L93-L103","doc":"**C2 (DEPENDENT on C1) — sector enumeration.**\n\nGiven the selection postulate, the electroweak carriers are exactly\n`k ∈ {2, 3, 4}`. The forward inclusion `carrier ⊆ {2,3,4}` follows from\nC1's window bound (proved as `ew_enumeration` /\n`sub_saturating_enumeration`); the conjectural content here is only the\n*reverse* inclusion — that all three are realised as carriers. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSelectionPrinciple.carrier_realised","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSelectionPrinciple.carrier_realised","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-higgs-torus-link-triplet.lean#L91-L91","doc":"The window is realised (non-vacuous): the `k = 2` (`W±`) link is a\ncarrier. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSelectionPrinciple.subSaturating","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSelectionPrinciple.subSaturating","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-higgs-torus-link-triplet.lean#L88-L88","doc":"Every carrier link is nontrivial (`genus = k-1 > 0`) and strictly\nbelow the genus-4 saturation (`genus < 4`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSelectionPrinciple.isCarrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSelectionPrinciple.isCarrier","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-higgs-torus-link-triplet.lean#L85-L85","doc":"Carrier predicate on the twist parameter `k` of `T(2, 2k)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSelectionPrinciple.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSelectionPrinciple.mk","kind":"ctor","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-higgs-torus-link-triplet.lean#L83-L83","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSelectionPrinciple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EWSelectionPrinciple","kind":"class","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/electroweak-higgs-torus-link-triplet.lean#L67-L91","doc":"**C1 (PRIMARY) — electroweak selection postulate.**\n\nThe electroweak carrier sector consists of the *nontrivial, strictly\nsub-saturating* even-twist 2-component torus links: those with Seifert\ngenus `g` in the window `0 < g < 4 = g(Σ₄)`, the sub-saturating complement\nof the genus-4-**saturating** carriers `{T(2,9), T(3,5)}` (corpus:\n`genus-filtration-ideal`).\n\n**This class now carries ONLY the physics selection postulate** — the\nclaim that the electroweak sector *is* realised by this window. The\n*enumeration* of the window (that it is exactly `{T(2,4),T(2,6),T(2,8)}`,\n`k ∈ {2,3,4}`) and the far-commuting minimality are no longer part of this\nconjecture: they are the proved `thm:ew-triplet-far-commuting-minimal` and\n`prop:electroweak-triplet-bring-embedding`. The field carries the window\nmembership as a parameter-quantified predicate, not the conclusion. ","signatureChunk":0}]}